"""/procedimientos/skinny-bbl — Spanish copy.

The page exists for one reader: someone already told she does not have enough
fat for a BBL. Two lines do that work and neither may be softened.

  "Le dijeron que no tenía suficiente grasa."
  Naming the rejection is the point. It is usually true of a conventional BBL
  and it is not the same as having nothing to work with.

  "Menos grasa significa menos margen, no menos operación."
  The recovery is identical to a full BBL — three months of compression and the
  same sitting restriction. Anyone reading "small" as "easier" is the person
  this page has to reach.

The safety paragraph is the same as on the full BBL page and is stated at every
volume: fat goes above the muscle, never into it, and injection into the gluteal
muscle caused the deaths that gave this operation its reputation.

"skinny BBL" stays in English. It is what patients search for and what he says
on camera; a Spanish coinage would be a term nobody uses.
"""

